   "source": [
    "## Model Selection\n",
    "\n",
    "LightGBM and CatBoost were selected as nonlinear candidates because 335 lagged,\n",
    "rolling, regime, and interaction-prone features are unlikely to relate linearly to\n",
    "the one-hour direction target. Both support regularization, stochastic subsampling,\n",
    "nonlinear thresholds, and efficient training on more than 200,000 observations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Separate models were evaluated for h4 (1 hour), h16 (4 hours), and h96 (24 hours).\n",
    "Model and probability-calibration choices were made with five-fold expanding\n",
    "walk-forward CV only. The 2024 holdout was diagnostic; the reserved 2025+ final test\n",
    "was not opened because no strategy passed the economic gate.\n",
    "\n",
    "Final statistical candidates were LightGBM + sigmoid calibration for h4, CatBoost +\n",
    "sigmoid for h16, and raw LightGBM probabilities for h96.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "Beyond raw OHLCV, the production feature set contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "- log/simple returns and momentum over 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, and 96 candles;\n",
    "- rolling statistics, moving-average distance/slope, RSI, MACD, and Bollinger features;\n",
    "- historical, Parkinson, Garman–Klass, and ATR-based volatility;\n",
    "- volume/trade rolling statistics, z-scores, taker-buy ratio, and imbalance;\n",
    "- candle body/range/wicks, gap indicators, and lagged versions;\n",
    "- cyclical UTC hour/weekday/month encodings and market-regime indicators.\n",
    "\n",
    "All features are causal and prefix-invariant. A 672-candle warm-up is removed, and\n",
    "validation confirmed no nulls, infinities, target/future columns, duplicate keys, or\n",
    "non-determinism. The binary h4 target is 1 when the future one-hour log return is\n",
    "greater than 0.1%. Targets are aligned by an explicit end timestamp.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
